;; The Vis extension CONTRACT, on its own — `com.blockether/vis-contract`.
;;
;; Everything an extension may ask the host for is DECLARED in
;; `resources/vis-contract/*.edn`; this project reads it, validates it and renders
;; it, and does nothing else. It requires no Vis namespace, so the engine, an
;; extension and a tool in somebody else's repository read one declaration without
;; dragging the whole agent along.
;;
;; `python/` is the same contract for the other ecosystem (`pip install
;; vis-contract`): the rendered `contract.json` and the host protocol both Python
;; hosts implement. One document, two registries, one version — VIS_VERSION.
{:deps {com.cnuernber/charred {:mvn/version "1.041"}
        org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version "1.12.5"}}
 :paths ["src" "resources"]}
